WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:17.752
This is the Daily Karma. Today’s practice is kintsugi: the golden seam. Find a supported position. Let your eyes close, or rest gently on the painting.

2
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.034
Notice the weight of your body being held. Let the tongue rest and the shoulders fall. Allow this moment to ask nothing from you.

3
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:07.288
Notice one breath arriving and one breath leaving. Do not improve it. Let each breath return you to the direct experience of this moment.

4
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:36.399
Kintsugi repairs broken pottery with gold. The crack is not concealed or made to look new. It is filled and traced, and becomes the most looked at part of the bowl.

5
00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:01.310
Picture the seam: a thin gold river running across the glaze. You can see exactly where it broke. The bowl is not pretending, and it still holds water.

6
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:30.774
Notice what your body is doing with these words. Soften around the eyes, the hands, and the belly. Keep only the effort needed to stay present.

7
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:57.056
Bring attention to something in you that healed. Do not open it. Let it simply be there, breathing, without being called damage.

8
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:26.449
For a little while, I will be quiet. Let thoughts pass like weather over a wide landscape. When attention wanders, return with patience.

9
00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:03.127
Still here. Still breathing. Nothing special needs to happen. This quiet awareness is already a useful way of meeting your life.

10
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:25.963
Let one repaired thing be visible today. An apology already made. A habit already changed. Let it count rather than hiding it.

11
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:53.820
Notice the sounds around you. Invite movement back into your hands and feet. Open your eyes softly. Thank you for meeting this day with Karma.
